    "directionalBusinessInterpretation": "The business map is a qualitative explanation, not an estimated profit or measured causal model. Every business relationship is declared context and uses certainty=hypothesis to avoid presenting the graph as a verified business finding. The basis distinguishes structural assumptions from uncertain business hypotheses. With a fixed staff pool, outreach removes capacity from the floor; a service decline is not inevitable while sufficient coverage remains. Customer response and its effect on revenue are uncertain. Effects describe direction at the target node, not whether a change is desirable; positive promotion-cost means more cost. Venue revenue is distinct from retained contribution: the article's contribution per additional guest is after the offer and relevant variable costs. Any lost contribution from discounts to existing customers is a separate deduction, counted once. Its conditional contribution comparison is not total venue profit. No coefficient, probability, outcome value or profit calculation is supplied.",
    "pointerConvention": "Source JSON pointers follow RFC 6901 and are relative to each referenced retained file. Report record paths address the losslessly expanded normalized assessment, not the encoded payload nodes. All file paths are relative to this file.",
    "resourceInterpretation": "The graph names a conceptual shared resource. The existing app uses aggregate qualifiedStaff, unavailableStaff, option promoters and the insideStaff consequence; native resources/bookings tables are empty. No individual scheduling or new capacity engine is implied.",
    "assessmentInterpretation": "Coverage records copy native insideStaff values and staffing-coverage/SUFFICIENCY findings for the declared situation. Passing this condition alone is not whole-plan feasibility, preference, financial return, managerial authorization or actual execution.",
    "reportingInterpretation": "The floor team and promoters report to Sam and influence the deployment through their declared priorities. Sam reports to the owner and alone makes the deployment decision within the spending and operating scope delegated to him. Reporting to the owner does not add an owner approval step to this decision. These are author-declared relationships, not app-assessed authority, authenticated identities or a multi-user governance feature."
  },
